1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,470
Dad's FD was growing every year,

2
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:06,506
yet Dad was getting poorer.

3
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:09,976
There is a thick file of receipts in the cupboard.

4
00:00:09,976 --> 00:00:12,578
Interest is written on every receipt.

5
00:00:12,578 --> 00:00:17,349
Dad touches it lovingly and says, son, it's safe,

6
00:00:17,349 --> 00:00:18,650
it won't go anywhere.

7
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:22,847
One evening Mummy came home with a bag of vegetables.

8
00:00:22,847 --> 00:00:27,509
The bag was light, but the bill was heavy. Mummy said,

9
00:00:27,509 --> 00:00:32,172
this same money used to last the whole week comfortably.

10
00:00:32,172 --> 00:00:36,835
Now it's finished by midweek. Dad took off his glasses,

11
00:00:36,835 --> 00:00:38,700
and went quiet.

12
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:42,683
Dad's calculation was perfectly simple. The money is in the bank,

13
00:00:42,683 --> 00:00:46,666
interest gets added every year, so the total is growing.

14
00:00:46,666 --> 00:00:49,056
The number on the receipt kept getting bigger.

15
00:00:49,056 --> 00:00:52,242
But at the shop, that same number kept falling short.

16
00:00:52,242 --> 00:00:55,030
This is the hidden thief in this story.

17
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:59,432
So today, three questions. First, you get interest on an FD,

18
00:00:59,432 --> 00:01:02,514
so how did the money still become less? Second,

19
00:01:02,514 --> 00:01:07,357
when and how much tax is cut on FD interest? Third,

20
00:01:07,357 --> 00:01:09,558
where should you keep your emergency money?

21
00:01:09,558 --> 00:01:13,520
The answers to all three are in this house's story.

22
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:18,364
First question. You got interest, so how did the money still become less?

23
00:01:18,364 --> 00:01:22,238
To understand this, you need to know one word: inflation.

24
00:01:22,238 --> 00:01:26,598
Inflation means prices of things slowly going up.

25
00:01:26,598 --> 00:01:29,504
The thali you buy today,

26
00:01:29,504 --> 00:01:32,410
next year the same thali will cost more.

27
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:34,706
Now look at the FD interest.

28
00:01:34,706 --> 00:01:41,136
In July 2026, banks gave an average of about 5.9 percent interest on new FDs.

29
00:01:41,136 --> 00:01:44,811
This is in a Grip Invest report.

30
00:01:44,811 --> 00:01:48,944
It sounds good. The money is growing,

31
00:01:48,944 --> 00:01:51,700
so everything is fine, right?

32
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:56,121
But the real question is this. How much did your money grow,

33
00:01:56,121 --> 00:01:59,560
and how much did your expenses grow? If the cost of milk,

34
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:04,472
medicine and school fees rises faster than the interest,

35
00:02:04,472 --> 00:02:07,420
then the number on the receipt is bigger,

36
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:11,350
but your buying power has become smaller.

37
00:02:11,350 --> 00:02:14,027
This is called real return.

38
00:02:14,027 --> 00:02:19,826
Real return means what is truly left after subtracting inflation from the interest.

39
00:02:19,826 --> 00:02:22,949
If inflation is less than 5.9 percent,

40
00:02:22,949 --> 00:02:26,517
then you are a little ahead. If it is more,

41
00:02:26,517 --> 00:02:29,640
So you are quietly following behind.

42
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:33,786
One day the son counted the coins in his piggy bank.

43
00:02:33,786 --> 00:02:37,933
Grandpa, meaning Papa, said, don't spend them, save them.

44
00:02:37,933 --> 00:02:39,775
The son asked, Grandpa,

45
00:02:39,775 --> 00:02:43,922
the toffee that last year you could get for these coins,

46
00:02:43,922 --> 00:02:47,147
why can't we get it now? Papa laughed it off,

47
00:02:47,147 --> 00:02:49,450
but the question was absolutely right.

48
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:53,395
Inflation is a hidden tax. Nobody fills out a form,

49
00:02:53,395 --> 00:02:55,149
no notice comes.

50
00:02:55,149 --> 00:02:59,971
It's just that every year your rupee loses a little of its value.

51
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:04,355
If the interest on an FD doesn't run faster than this thief,

52
00:03:04,355 --> 00:03:08,300
then the money looks safe, but keeps shrinking.

53
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:12,950
This was never written in Papa's file.

54
00:03:12,950 --> 00:03:16,331
The receipt only shows the interest, not the inflation.

55
00:03:16,331 --> 00:03:19,712
That's why Papa felt everything was growing.

56
00:03:19,712 --> 00:03:25,630
In reality, his FD was just running to stay in the same place.

57
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:29,781
The second question, and here is another hidden cost.

58
00:03:29,781 --> 00:03:32,548
The interest on an FD is not free.

59
00:03:32,548 --> 00:03:35,315
It gets added to your income.

60
00:03:35,315 --> 00:03:40,388
And income is taxed according to your slab.

61
00:03:40,388 --> 00:03:45,000
Slab means a ladder of income: the higher you go, the more tax.

62
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,822
My sister came home from the office and opened her FD statement on her phone.

63
00:03:50,822 --> 00:03:55,585
The interest was credited, but not in full. She asked,

64
00:03:55,585 --> 00:03:59,290
why did less come in? The answer was TDS.

65
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:06,170
TDS means the bank itself deducts your tax and sends it to the government.

66
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:11,596
My sister thought this was the whole tax. But that's not necessarily so.

67
00:04:11,596 --> 00:04:14,555
TDS is only an advance deduction.

68
00:04:14,555 --> 00:04:18,501
The final calculation is done in the income tax return.

69
00:04:18,501 --> 00:04:20,967
If your slab is high,

70
00:04:20,967 --> 00:04:25,900
you may have to pay more tax when you file your return.

71
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:28,272
Now think about the highest slab.

72
00:04:28,272 --> 00:04:32,621
In the new regime, the highest slab has 30 percent tax.

73
00:04:32,621 --> 00:04:36,575
That means 30 percent of the FD interest goes to the government.

74
00:04:36,575 --> 00:04:40,133
The interest that was already fighting inflation

75
00:04:40,133 --> 00:04:42,110
became even thinner.

76
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:45,907
So this is the real calculation of an FD. First tax is cut,

77
00:04:45,907 --> 00:04:47,806
then inflation eats into it. Whatever is left,

78
00:04:47,806 --> 00:04:50,844
that is the money you have truly earned.

79
00:04:50,844 --> 00:04:56,160
For many people, this remaining portion turns out much smaller than expected.

80
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:00,702
But not everyone pays this much tax. Papa is retired,

81
00:05:00,702 --> 00:05:02,353
Their income is low.

82
00:05:02,353 --> 00:05:06,069
Under the new regime, on income up to 12 lakh,

83
00:05:06,069 --> 00:05:08,960
after the rebate, the tax comes to zero.

84
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:11,850
Rebate means a discount given by the government.

85
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:17,651
That means for people like Papa, the tax burden can get lighter.

86
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:21,668
But the thief called inflation is still standing right there.

87
00:05:21,668 --> 00:05:26,130
Even if there is no tax, expenses still keep going up.

88
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:29,700
So don't look only at tax, look at the real return.

89
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,462
And one more useful thing.

90
00:05:31,462 --> 00:05:33,929
If your income is within the exemption limit,

91
00:05:33,929 --> 00:05:36,044
but the bank has deducted TDS,

92
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:39,568
that money can come back to you when you file your return.

93
00:05:39,568 --> 00:05:42,035
Many people never claim it.

94
00:05:42,035 --> 00:05:44,150
Their money just lies there.

95
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:47,383
Third question. So is FD useless? Not at all.

96
00:05:47,383 --> 00:05:49,898
Everything has its own job.

97
00:05:49,898 --> 00:05:52,053
The job of an FD is less about growing money,

98
00:05:52,053 --> 00:05:54,208
and more about keeping money safe.

99
00:05:54,208 --> 00:05:58,160
And there is one place where an FD does this job very well.

100
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:01,405
One night Papa had chest pain.

101
00:06:01,405 --> 00:06:05,056
At the hospital, the first question was, how much deposit will you pay?

102
00:06:05,056 --> 00:06:09,519
At that time, we could not wait for any long scheme.

103
00:06:09,519 --> 00:06:13,170
We needed the money that very night, without any delay.

104
00:06:13,170 --> 00:06:15,765
This is what is called an emergency fund.

105
00:06:15,765 --> 00:06:21,386
An emergency fund is money kept only for hard times.

106
00:06:21,386 --> 00:06:23,549
If you lose your job, if illness comes,

107
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:26,576
or if a sudden expense comes up at home.

108
00:06:26,576 --> 00:06:30,900
This money's job is not to earn, but to be available on time.

109
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:34,750
This is where an FD or a savings account helps.

110
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:39,080
The money can be taken out quickly, and its value doesn't go up and down.

111
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:41,005
Inflation will eat a little, agreed.

112
00:06:41,005 --> 00:06:48,223
But the value of getting money instantly in an emergency is far more than that small loss.

113
00:06:48,223 --> 00:06:51,110
You also get to sleep at night.

114
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:54,078
And what if the bank itself goes under?

115
00:06:54,078 --> 00:06:56,623
This is where the name DICGC comes in.

116
00:06:56,623 --> 00:07:00,439
DICGC is the organisation that provides insurance on bank deposits.

117
00:07:00,439 --> 00:07:03,408
For every depositor, in each bank,

118
00:07:03,408 --> 00:07:06,800
cover is given up to 5 lakh rupees.

119
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:11,095
So Wife made a simple rule for the house.

120
00:07:11,095 --> 00:07:14,912
Don't keep the whole emergency money in just one bank,

121
00:07:14,912 --> 00:07:18,252
If needed, spread it across different banks.

122
00:07:18,252 --> 00:07:22,070
So that your money stays within the cover everywhere.

123
00:07:22,070 --> 00:07:25,410
This isn't fear, it's just being sensible.

124
00:07:25,410 --> 00:07:28,652
An FD works fine for small goals too.

125
00:07:28,652 --> 00:07:30,454
Next year's school fees for the child,

126
00:07:30,454 --> 00:07:34,417
or a wedding expense a few months away. When you need the money soon,

127
00:07:34,417 --> 00:07:38,740
taking the risk of a place that goes up and down is not sensible.

128
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:41,829
Now, the mistake Papa made,

129
00:07:41,829 --> 00:07:46,242
and many people make. The mistake was not taking an FD.

130
00:07:46,242 --> 00:07:47,124
The mistake was

131
00:07:47,124 --> 00:07:51,537
keeping a whole life's savings only in FDs for years and years.

132
00:07:51,537 --> 00:07:55,950
Treating long-term money like emergency money too.

133
00:07:55,950 --> 00:08:00,163
Over the long run, inflation cuts a little every year.

134
00:08:00,163 --> 00:08:02,035
On top of that, tax too.

135
00:08:02,035 --> 00:08:06,247
Year after year, these small cuts keep adding up.

136
00:08:06,247 --> 00:08:11,396
And one day Mummy asks, where did the money go? The answer is,

137
00:08:11,396 --> 00:08:12,800
quietly, slowly.

138
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,729
So what should we do? First step,

139
00:08:14,729 --> 00:08:17,816
divide your savings according to the work each part has to do.

140
00:08:17,816 --> 00:08:20,902
Some money is needed right away, some after years.

141
00:08:20,902 --> 00:08:23,217
Keeping both in the same place

142
00:08:23,217 --> 00:08:26,690
is like opening every lock with one key.

143
00:08:26,690 --> 00:08:32,149
Second step, work out your real return yourself every year. Look at the interest,

144
00:08:32,149 --> 00:08:37,112
subtract the tax, and think about how much your household expenses have gone up.

145
00:08:37,112 --> 00:08:40,586
If what's left is very small,

146
00:08:40,586 --> 00:08:44,060
then at least do ask questions.

147
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:49,735
Third step, understand other options for long-term goals. Like PPF,

148
00:08:49,735 --> 00:08:55,927
which is a government scheme and currently gives 7.1 percent interest per year.

149
00:08:55,927 --> 00:09:01,086
Every option has its own lock-in, risk and tax.

150
00:09:01,086 --> 00:09:03,150
First understand, then think.

151
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:04,990
This is not investment advice.

152
00:09:04,990 --> 00:09:07,935
Before putting your money anywhere, look at your needs,

153
00:09:07,935 --> 00:09:09,407
age and risk.

154
00:09:09,407 --> 00:09:12,719
If needed, talk to a qualified advisor.

155
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:18,240
The only aim is that you can see the truth behind the number on the receipt.

156
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:21,426
That night Papa opened the file,

157
00:09:21,426 --> 00:09:26,737
and for the first time kept the vegetable bill next to the receipt.

158
00:09:26,737 --> 00:09:32,579
He looked at both, and said softly, being safe and growing

159
00:09:32,579 --> 00:09:37,890
are different things. Nobody told me this earlier.

160
00:09:37,890 --> 00:09:39,972
Now, one simple question for you.

161
00:09:39,972 --> 00:09:43,719
Where is the most of your household's savings kept,

162
00:09:43,719 --> 00:09:48,298
In an FD or somewhere else? Write it in the comments in one word.

163
00:09:48,298 --> 00:09:50,380
I read every reply.

164
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:54,928
In the next video, another story from the home. Gold,

165
00:09:54,928 --> 00:10:00,993
which is kept somewhere in every mother's cupboard.

166
00:10:00,993 --> 00:10:05,036
Does it really protect you from rising prices,

167
00:10:05,036 --> 00:10:08,573
or is that also a sweet misunderstanding?

168
00:10:08,573 --> 00:10:11,100
See you in the next story.
